;;;; colon-z-ed-output.expected-failures.lisp
;;;;
;;;; Known failures for the deftests generated from
;;;; colon-z-ed-output.test.
;;;;
;;;; Initially auto-generated by
;;;;   (fortran-format::establish-baseline-expected-failures ...)
;;;; but maintained by hand thereafter: remove a name when its
;;;; bug is fixed.
;;;;
;;;; The 175 entries below are (:, Zw) tests of small negative
;;;; values at widths 8-10.  Same root cause as the standalone Z
;;;; corpus's failures: the corpus expects 32-bit-host hex
;;;; ("FFFFFFFF"), but on a 64-bit host *boz-word-bits* = 64 emits
;;;; 16 hex digits which overflow widths 8-10.  Colon doesn't
;;;; affect Z output (it only terminates when values run out, which
;;;; never happens with one value), so these track the plain
;;;; z-ed-output expected failures.

